The binary embeds iPXE (https://ipxe.org/) as snponly.efi, licensed under the GNU General Public License,
version 2 (with the iPXE UBDL exception). Its complete corresponding source is upstream iPXE at the commit in
mgmt/ipxe/IPXE_COMMIT plus the changes in mgmt/ipxe/patches/ (also GPLv2 / UBDL); mgmt/ipxe/build.sh fetches,
patches and builds it. iPXE is not covered by the Apache License above.

mgmt/ipxe/signed/ holds unmodified official iPXE release binaries (Secure Boot builds): snponly.efi, signed by the
iPXE Secure Boot CA (UBDL), and the iPXE shim (https://github.com/ipxe/shim, BSD-2-Clause) signed by Microsoft.

broom-stage.tar.gz (published on the Releases page, downloaded by the binary for Windows images) holds a Linux
kernel, an initrd and a shim made of unmodified Ubuntu binaries: the Linux kernel, busybox, ntfs-3g, wget,
efibootmgr, util-linux, dosfstools and others, under their own licenses (mostly GPL-2.0 / GPL-3.0), and shim
(BSD-2-Clause). SOURCES.txt inside the bundle lists every package with its exact version and source package; the
corresponding source is in the Ubuntu archive (`apt-get source <package>=<version>`, or
https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/<package>/<version>). These are not covered by the Apache License above.
